# Family Calendar Project

Flutter + Node 24 app replacing a wall kiosk eCalendar. Read `project-description..txt` and `AGENTS.md` for full context.

## Stack

- **app/** — Flutter, two flavors: `kiosk` (landscape, read-only) and `mobile` (portrait, Firebase App Distro). **Android APKs built on bering-dev**; iOS on Mac
- **server/** — Node 24 on bering-dev, PM2, Postgres, `/api/v1` routes
- **Auth** — Password + long-lived JWT; kiosk uses device token; Google OAuth only on mobile

## Non-negotiables

- Kiosk never calls Google APIs directly — server aggregates calendars
- Wall: 7×5 grid, current week at top, scroll with idle reset, day tap popup, landscape only
- Phones: link Google accounts, nickname + color per calendar; all views read-only
- One shared family password; kiosk pairs via server URL + 6-char code from mobile
- Google sync: poll every 1 minute on server
- Family-only distribution; no app stores

## When adding features

1. Check product constraints in `project-description..txt`
2. Prefer server-side sync/cache over client-side Google calls
3. Keep kiosk and mobile in one Flutter project via flavors, not duplicate apps
